1
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:09,870
The game has changed.

2
00:08:07,741 --> 00:08:13,741
TRON: Legacy is a adventure, action, science fiction
film directed by Joseph Kosinski.

3
00:12:11,612 --> 00:12:17,612
Sam Flynn, the tech-savvy and daring son of Kevin Flynn, investigates
his father's disappearance and is pulled into The Grid.

4
00:16:15,483 --> 00:16:21,483
With the help of a mysterious program named Quorra, Sam quests to stop
evil dictator Clu from crossing into the real world.

5
00:20:19,354 --> 00:20:25,354
Sam Flynn, played by Garrett Hedlund.

6
00:24:23,225 --> 00:24:29,225
Quorra, played by Olivia Wilde.

7
00:28:27,096 --> 00:28:33,096
Kevin Flynn / Clu, played by Jeff Bridges.

8
00:32:30,967 --> 00:32:36,967
Alan Bradley / Tron, played by Bruce Boxleitner.

9
00:36:34,838 --> 00:36:40,838
Jarvis, played by James Frain.

10
00:40:38,709 --> 00:40:44,709
Gem, played by Beau Garrett.

11
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:48,580
Tron: Legacy is a 2010 American science fiction action film directed by
Joseph Kosinski, and written by Adam Horowitz and Edward Kitsis.

12
00:48:46,451 --> 00:48:52,451
It is the second installment in the Tron series and a sequel to Tron (1982).

13
00:52:50,322 --> 00:52:56,322
The film stars Jeff Bridges, Garrett Hedlund, Olivia
Wilde, Bruce Boxleitner, and Michael Sheen.

14
00:56:54,193 --> 00:57:00,193
The story follows Kevin Flynn's adult son Sam, who responds to a message from his long-lost father and is transported into a virtual reality
called "the Grid", where Sam, his father, and the algorithm Quorra must stop the malevolent program Clu from invading the real world.

15
01:00:58,064 --> 01:01:04,064
Interest in creating a sequel to Tron arose after
the film garnered a cult following.

16
01:05:01,935 --> 01:05:07,935
After much speculation, Walt Disney Pictures began a concerted effort in 2005 to devise a
sequel, with the hiring of Brian Klugman and Lee Sternthal as writers.

17
01:09:05,806 --> 01:09:11,806
Kosinski was recruited as director two years later.

18
01:13:09,677 --> 01:13:15,677
As he was not optimistic about Disney's The Matrix-esque approach to the film, Kosinski filmed a concept trailer, which
he used to conceptualize the universe of Tron: Legacy and convince the studio to greenlight the film.

19
01:17:13,548 --> 01:17:19,548
Principal photography took place in Vancouver over 67 days, in
and around the city's central business district.

20
01:21:17,419 --> 01:21:23,419
Most sequences were shot in 3D and ten companies were
involved with the extensive visual effects work.

21
01:25:21,290 --> 01:25:27,290
Chroma keying and other techniques were used to
allow more freedom in creating effects.

22
01:29:25,161 --> 01:29:31,161
Daft Punk composed the musical score, incorporating their
trademark electronic music with orchestral sounds.

23
01:33:29,032 --> 01:33:35,032
Tron: Legacy premiered in Tokyo on November 30, 2010, and was released in the
United States on December 17, by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures.

24
01:37:32,903 --> 01:37:38,903
Disney vigorously promoted the film across multiple media platforms, including
merchandising, consumer products, theme parks, and advertising.

25
01:41:36,774 --> 01:41:42,774
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and was a commercial
success, grossing $410 million against a $170 million budget.

26
01:45:40,645 --> 01:45:46,645
The film was nominated for Best Sound Editing at the 83rd Academy Awards.

27
01:49:44,516 --> 01:49:50,516
Like its predecessor, Tron: Legacy has been
described as a cult film since its release.

28
01:53:48,387 --> 01:53:54,387
A further sequel, Tron: Ares, was released in 2025.

29
01:57:52,258 --> 01:57:58,258
The film explores themes of artificial intelligence (a.i.),
computer program, secret identity, dystopia, simulation.

30
02:01:56,129 --> 02:02:02,129
The tone is thought_provoking.
